x86_64-linux  clang emits only the C2 and D2 variants of a constructor and destructor that a class template's instantiation defines - vague linkage, as for one defined inside its class - where cxx1 emits C1 beside C2 and D1 beside D2, as it does for all of them. move-constructor.nonames and implicit-move.nonames record the same difference. The two are identical for a class with no virtual bases; arm64-darwin and x86_64-windows agree on every name.
